description.narrative:
The project aims to increase media literacy education and media skills for 500 young people from local districts to understand, analyze, share knowledge and advocate among their community the values of correct information.



 Media literacy education is a rising priority globally to the problem of misinformation and false news. In Moldova, this is becoming increasingly prominent and the authorities failure to control false information. It seems that misinformation is widely used as a solid tool for political manipulation by state actors. This indicates that society does not understand critical opinions and school does not form skills of critical thinking in relation to the media, so it's obvious the lack of knowledge in media literacy in Moldova. Nowadays the impact of media has increased, especially on young people.



 Project immediate outputs include:

 1)	More than 500 young people (including at least 20 your women in vulnerable position) and 20 your organizations and centers trained from 20 different districts. The participants learn critical media thinking; 

 2)	one study visit for 20 young people to different media organizations;

 3)	5 informative-educational educational short video about the importance of young people's attention regarding media literacy and the impact of false media messages; 

 4)	10 advocacy campaigns organized in district centers by youth organizations/centres; 

 5)	24 press releases and min. 50 posts on social media CDEC page about the project activities 

 6)	3 events (online/offline) about launching the project, study presentation and evaluation table of the project activities;



 The direct project beneficiaries are 500 young people aged 14-25 y., regardless of gender, ethnicity, physical disability, religion, different minority groups from local districts and 20 youth organizations and centers from local districts;



 The project is implemented by the Centre for Educational and Community Development (CDEC) that was founded in early 2017. CDEC has been actively involved in educational projects for young people and citizens from regions and rural areas. The experts from the leading media organization in Moldova, Independent Journalism Center, join the project as trainers. 



 The FLC grant for this project is 29 955 EUR. The total project budget is 32 355 EUR.
